      <details class="sc-faq" open>
      <summary>What is WLCSP?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Wafer level chip-scale packaging — the package is completed at wafer level and then singulated, so the finished part is essentially the die with a bump array, attached straight to the board.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>What does Hana's WLCSP flow include?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Incoming inspection, back-grind and dicing, die-attach film, flip-chip and WLCSP attach down to 80 µm Cu pillar bump pitch, wafer-level test, and singulation to tape and reel.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>Does Hana do wafer bumping or RDL?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">No. Bumping and redistribution-layer (RDL) processing stay at your foundry or bumping house. Hana takes over on arrival: back-grind, dicing, die-attach film, flip-chip and WLCSP attach down to 80 µm Cu pillar bump pitch, wafer-level test and packing.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>When is WLCSP the right choice?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">When footprint and profile are the binding constraints — mobile, wearable and other space-constrained products that attach the part directly to the board.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>How is WLP controlled?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
